  "items": [
    {
      "name": "Where the smell starts",
      "char_file": "샴푸_illust.jpg",
      "body": [
        "Scalp odor comes from",
        "buildup of skin cells,",
        "sweat and sebum",
        "",
        "Microbes break it down",
        "into the compounds you smell"
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "Washing the hair, not the scalp",
      "char_file": "샴푸_illust.jpg",
      "body": [
        "Lather that runs over",
        "the lengths and ends",
        "",
        "barely reaches the roots,",
        "where the odor is",
        "actually produced"
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "Washing — the fix",
      "char_file": "샴푸_illust.jpg",
      "body": [
        "Part the hair and work",
        "lather into the scalp itself"
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "A damp scalp overnight",
      "char_file": "베개_illust.jpg",
      "body": [
        "Fungi and bacteria thrive",
        "in warm, moist places",
        "",
        "A wet head on a pillow",
        "for eight hours is",
        "exactly that"
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "Drying — the fix",
      "char_file": "베개_illust.jpg",
      "body": [
        "Dry the scalp, not just",
        "the hair, before sleeping"
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "Sweat left under a cap",
      "char_file": "모자_illust.jpg",
      "body": [
        "Hours under a cap",
        "or helmet keep sweat",
        "warm against the skin",
        "",
        "and the cap itself",
        "holds onto it"
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "Caps — the fix",
      "char_file": "모자_illust.jpg",
      "body": [
        "Rinse the roots after",
        "sweating, and wash the cap"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "closing": {
    "headline": [
      [
        "Washing daily is fine —",
        "an oily scalp may need it"
      ],
      [
        "What matters more is where",
        "the lather goes, and how dry",
        "your scalp is at bedtime"
      ]
